{"content":[{"c":["ASAIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Royal servant sent by King Josiah of Judah to ask the prophetess Huldah about the meaning of the Book of the Law found in the renovation of the temple (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.12,14","r":"2Kgs.22.12,14","rawR":"2Kgs.22.12,14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.12,14","value":"2Kgs.22.12,14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:12, 14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.20","r":"2Chr.34.20","rawR":"2Chr.34.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.20","value":"2Chr.34.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Clan leader of Simeon’s tribe who settled in Gedor (Gerar?) during Hezekiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.36","r":"1Chr.4.36","rawR":"1Chr.4.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.36","value":"1Chr.4.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Levitical leader in the time of King David. Asaiah helped bring the ark to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.30","r":"1Chr.6.30","rawR":"1Chr.6.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.30","value":"1Chr.6.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.6,11","r":"1Chr.15.6,11","rawR":"1Chr.15.6,11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.6,11","value":"1Chr.15.6,11"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:6, 11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Shiloni’s oldest son. Asaiah’s family was among the first to resettle in Jerusalem after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.5","r":"1Chr.9.5","rawR":"1Chr.9.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.5","value":"1Chr.9.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:5"},"). Perhaps the same as Maaseiah of ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.5","r":"Neh.11.5","rawR":"Neh.11.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.5","value":"Neh.11.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 11:5"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Maaseiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Maaseiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Maaseiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Maaseiah #14"},"."],"sourceClass":"li